## Phase 6 — Abuse & Cost Controls

Each inbound WhatsApp message can trigger a full LLM-backed triage pipeline run. This is currently unprotected.

1. Add a per-phone-number rate limit on the webhook (e.g. max N messages per minute — reuse whatever rate-limiting pattern, if any, already secures other public endpoints in this codebase; if none exists, implement a simple token bucket keyed by phone number, persisted the same way as Phase 4's retry state).
2. When rate-limited, return a TwiML response with no pipeline execution — just log it, don't send an extra WhatsApp message back (to avoid making the spam problem worse).
3. Add a test simulating a burst of messages from one number and confirming the pipeline only runs the allowed number of times.
4. Double check `validate_signature`'s failure path can't be bypassed by omitting the header entirely when `ENV != development` — add an explicit test if Phase 1 didn't already cover this exact case.

**Exit criteria:** a burst of 50 messages from one number in under a minute does not trigger 50 pipeline executions.

